b.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-19T00:05:03Z","updated_at":"2024-10-19T00:05:03Z","body":"Seems that MinGW is doing some strange stuff with the code (again), i tested the mrp and in a build made with MSVC and the code works as expected, but compiled with MinGW has a strange behavior:\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.dev.custom_build [4631a617e], MSVC with production=yes:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad1d046d-be91-4078-84a1-07a4107d57a8\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.dev.custom_build [4631a617e], MinGW with production=yes lto=none\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/789e4dfd-bf9e-49af-b817-97eab73a0f16\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.dev3.official [f4af8201b]\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/accae297-a0ef-4026-857e-3858420e077a\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nGodot v4.4.dev3.official [f4af8201b] with `loop = false`\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be75b3d2-e977-43c0-9a5d-04d57c60c3f5\r\n\r\n\r\nMaybe my compiled version with MinGW doesn't reproduce the bug in the same way like the official builds because the `lto=none` or maybe because the MinGW version (14.1.0 in my case) but using the official builds i reproduce the bug in the same way the issue shows. Also commenting the code that starts the video seems to make the timer work as expected in my self compiled build with MinGW.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2423390494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2423397234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98302#issuecomment-2423397234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98302","id":2423397234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Qchty","user":{"login":"caioraphael1","id":58512144,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTEyMTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58512144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1","html_url":"https://github.com/caioraphael1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/caioraphael1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-19T00:15:57Z","updated_at":"2024-10-19T00:15:57Z","body":"I'm not able to see any of the videos you've sent. I suppose you encoded the videos with H.265 (HEVC)? I tried that once and had the same issue.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2423397234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2423728259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98302#issuecomment-2423728259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98302","id":2423728259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QdyiD","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-19T09:48:08Z","updated_at":"2024-10-19T09:48:08Z","body":"> I suppose you encoded the videos with H.265 (HEVC)?\r\n\r\nYes, strange that i can see normally in my pc and phone. \r\n\r\nBut anyways, here what happens in my compiled build with MinGW:\r\n\r\n```\r\nStarting\r\n10\r\n9.96600733333333\r\n9.94934066666667\r\n9.94019966666667\r\n9.94007104166223\r\n9.93882166666667\r\n9.93333333333333\r\n9.92777777777778\r\n9.92777777777778\r\n9.91096377777778\r\n9.89463577777778\r\n9.89463577777778\r\n9.87717377777778\r\n9.87717377777778\r\n9.85964777777778\r\n9.84334977777777\r\n9.84334977777777\r\n9.82669577777777\r\n0\r\n\r\n\r\nFinished!\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2423728259/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2445582755","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98302#issuecomment-2445582755","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98302","id":2445582755,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RxKGj","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-30T00:47:06Z","updated_at":"2024-10-30T00:54:41Z","body":"I took a look on the code related to `SceneTreeTimer` today and found something\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/08f9cba0fbf27f171dea55de6f8274928b9f0d84/scene/main/scene_tree.cpp#L568-L602\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nHere `p_time` is used to process the timers and tweens, and for some reason between `_process(false)` and `_flush_ugc()` `p_time` can receive a strange number (which make `SceneTreeTimer.time_left` become that big number) or become a NaN (which makes `SceneTreeTimer.time_left` imediatly go to zero). Here a video that shows the bug hapenning, notice that `process_time` always keep normal ([Youtube link](https://youtu.be/jqhpkVzcjTM) for anyone that can't see the video here):\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ac41c01-2fae-4a48-8ae3-75c56c64461c\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\r\nNow if instead pass `p_time` for `process_timers` and `process_tweens` we pass `process_time` the bug simply dissapear, even `p_time` keep the normal value ([Youtube link](https://youtu.be/3N9J5XORovM)):\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c090269-4c27-4c4b-9212-e8de1ce0d4b8\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nAnother test i did was create a double variable in `SceneTree.h` and create a const double inside `SceneTree::process` to check if they also would break and that's what happens ([Youtube link](https://youtu.be/zbHftAO0IXs)):\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/701e7df4-c6c7-416c-8e44-3781087f2c74\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\nAll the tests was made using Godot 08f9cba0f and compiling using MinGW with `production=yes` `lto=none` `debug_symbols=yes` (as said in my first commentary MSVC don't have this issue)\r\n\r\nUse `process_time` as parameter to call `process_timers` and `process_tweens` works but seems like hiding another bug so i wanted some insight before do anything else. @timothyqiu any idea why this is happening?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2445582755/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676164406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98302#issuecomment-2676164406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98302","id":2676164406,"node_id":"IC_kwD